dia-dgx-spark-lab!"},"196":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-19","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#contributing-to-the-documentation","content":"All changes to documentation must follow the same rigor as code changes."},"197":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-20","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#quick-start","content":"Bazel (primary):"},"198":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-21","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#quick-start","content":"Classic scripts (the `manage-docs.sh` wrapper installs npm dependencies when missing):"},"199":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-22","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#quick-start","content":"Inside `docs-site/` the same things are npm scripts: `npm run dev`, `npm run build`,\n`npm run visual`, `npm run nav:check`.  Screenshot baselines are refreshed with\n`bazelisk run //docs-site:visual-linux -- --update` (needs Docker), which renders them in the\nLinux image that matches the docs CI job — never on a laptop.  See `bazelisk run //docs:status`\nor the `--help` output for all options."},"200":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-23","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#information-architecture","content":"Sidebar groups live in `docs-site/lib/nav.json`, transcribed once from the former\n`mkdocs.yml` nav.  That file is gone, so `nav.json` is the source of truth: edit it by hand\nand verify with `npm run nav:check` (which fails if an entry has no page on disk).  The\ngroups are:"},"201":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-24","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#information-architecture","content":"**Home** — path cards, default stack, safety table"},"202":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-25","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#information-architecture","content":"**Start** — gold path, topology, profiles, learn-the-lab"},"203":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-26","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#information-architecture","content":"**Concepts** — architecture, NCCL, Resource Guard, stacks, glossary"},"204":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-27","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#information-architecture","content":"**Operate** — catalogs, dashboard, runbooks, troubleshooting"},"205":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-28","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#information-architecture","content":"**Reference** — project conventions, docs contributing, generated shell + dashboard API"},"206":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-29","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#information-architecture","content":"**Contribute** — dev environment, Bazel"},"207":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-30","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#information-architecture","content":"Every major section has an `index.md`. Keep existing published slugs (`getting-started`,\n`architecture`, …): the route is the file path without its extension, so renaming a file\nbreaks every bookmark and README link to it. Put **new** pages under `start/`, `learn/`,\n`concepts/`, `operate/`, `contribute/`."},"208":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-31","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#information-architecture","content":"A new page needs three things or it will not appear in the sidebar and the coverage gate\nfails: the file under `docs/`, an entry in the nav (see above), and a listing in\n`_HAND_WRITTEN_MD` in `docs/BUILD.bazel` so Bazel ships it as a runfile."},"209":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-32","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#information-architecture","content":"Use the right-hand ToC for long pages. Keep navigation focused."},"210":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-33","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#content-guidelines","content":"Every page must open (after the title or any intentional top widget such as the interactive panel) with a scannable overview in this bullet-point format:\n**What's on this page**"},"211":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-34","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#content-guidelines","content":"Bullets describing the main content, sections, diagrams, tables, etc.\n**What this enables / practical use**"},"212":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-35","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#content-guidelines","content":"Bullets describing reader benefit, common use cases, or what the content lets you achieve.\nWrite those labels as bold markdown plus lists, not as JSX. The site wraps the first pair into a two-column panel; later examples on the same page stay ordinary prose."},"213":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-36","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#content-guidelines","content":"Write for humans. Be concise. Remove filler."},"214":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-37","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#content-guidelines","content":"Include copy-pasteable examples."},"215":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-38","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#content-guidelines","content":"Use Mermaid for diagrams (supported)."},"216":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-39","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#content-guidelines","content":"Prefer `<Callout type=\"info|warning|error\" title=\"…\">` for asides and `<Tabs>`/`<Tab>` for\nalternatives. The `!!!` and `=== \"Title\"` syntax is **not** parsed any more — the migration\nrewrote existing uses, and new content uses the components directly (see\n`docs-site/components/mdx-components.tsx` for what is importable)."},"217":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-40","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#content-guidelines","content":"Pages that need those components are `.mdx`; pages that do not can stay `.md`. Both are\nvalid MDX, so plain Markdown keeps working unchanged."},"218":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-41","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#content-guidelines","content":"Escape what MDX would otherwise read as JSX: a literal `<` in prose or code needs `&lt;`,\nand `{`/`}` outside a code fence must be `&#123;`/`&#125;`."},"219":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-42","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#content-guidelines","content":"Always link to source code or exact commands when possible."},"220":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-43","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs"