-one-200-gbs-qsfp-cable","content":"Existing 1-node / 2-node Jobs and `group_vars` document:"},"3371":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-28","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#2-node-pair-one-200-gbs-qsfp-cable","content":"Also typically `NCCL_IB_DISABLE=0`, `NCCL_P2P_DISABLE=0`, `NCCL_SHM_DISABLE=0`. Confirm names with `ibdev2netdev` on **your** nodes before baking env."},"3372":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-29","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#2-node-pair-one-200-gbs-qsfp-cable","content":"kimi / kimi-test omit `hostNetwork` (isolation). Heavy Ray / GLM-5.2 Jobs set `hostNetwork: true` (and GLM `hostIPC: true`) so IFNAME is visible."},"3373":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-30","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#3-node-qsfp-ring-mode-b-and-mode-c","content":"200 Gb/s per physical port — not NVLink, not an IB switch. Triangle:"},"3374":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-31","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#3-node-qsfp-ring-mode-b-and-mode-c","content":"Port0 = cage next to the RJ-45 jack; Port1 = far cage. Wrong polarity looks half-alive."},"3375":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-32","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#3-node-qsfp-ring-mode-b-and-mode-c","content":"Mode B (GLM-5.3-Flash TP=3) and Mode C (DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash TP=3) Jobs set:"},"3376":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-33","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#3-node-qsfp-ring-mode-b-and-mode-c","content":"Plus `hostNetwork: true` and `hostIPC: true`. If 10GbE is not `enP7s7`, set `LAB_MGMT_IFNAME`. Mode C also cuts `NCCL_BUFFSIZE=1MiB`."},"3377":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-34","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#3-node-qsfp-ring-mode-b-and-mode-c","content":"`highspeed_interfaces: enp1s0f0np0,enp1s0f1np1` is the pair reference. Ring Jobs in `k8s/workloads/glm-5.3-flash/` and `deepseek-v4.1-flash/` already have the ring block."},"3378":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-35","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#3-node-qsfp-ring-mode-b-and-mode-c","content":"Full cabling, aliases, and util caps: LiteLLM rounded stack."},"3379":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-36","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#4--5-nodes--mikrotik-crs804-4ddq-hrm-switch","content":"The switch fabric is a managed 4× 400G QSFP-DD device; each node sees **one** RoCE link:"},"3380":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-37","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#4--5-nodes--mikrotik-crs804-4ddq-hrm-switch","content":"**4 nodes:** one full CRS804 port per node (`sfpplus1`…`sfpplus4`). The Spark CX-7 link is 200 Gb/s."},"3381":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-38","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#4--5-nodes--mikrotik-crs804-4ddq-hrm-switch","content":"**5 nodes:** three full ports + one port split with a breakout cable into\n`sfpplus4a` / `sfpplus4b` (two 200G lanes). Both lanes must be declared in the\n`switch.port_map` — the topology validator rejects a lone lane."},"3382":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-39","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#4--5-nodes--mikrotik-crs804-4ddq-hrm-switch","content":"Each link is its own /24 (192.168.110–114, MTU 9000) from the generated per-node\nnetplan — one node per subnet, so there is no shared-suffix IP scheme to get wrong."},"3383":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-40","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#4--5-nodes--mikrotik-crs804-4ddq-hrm-switch","content":"`NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME` stays the management NIC; the payload rides the single RoCE HCA\n(`NCCL_IB_HCA` from live `ibdev2netdev` names per node)."},"3384":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-41","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#4--5-nodes--mikrotik-crs804-4ddq-hrm-switch","content":"Heavy Jobs use `hostNetwork: true`. Do not assume the 2-node pair\n`NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME` list is complete — it is not, on a switch."},"3385":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-42","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#4--5-nodes--mikrotik-crs804-4ddq-hrm-switch","content":"The switch block (host, read-only user, `port_map`) lives in `lab.yaml`; the password is\n`LAB_SWITCH_PASSWORD` in the operator's environment only. Qwen 3.5 397B NVFP4 is the\ncanonical TP=4 Job here. Cabling and port map: Choose topology."},"3386":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-43","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#verify","content":"After `start-test` on a pair:"},"3387":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-44","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#verify","content":"Expect the high-speed IFNAME in the NCCL init lines, not the management NIC as payload."},"3388":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-45","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#verify","content":"If logs show fallback to `eth0` / 10GbE for all-reduce, stop the Job (`bazelisk run //:manage -- stop`) and fix netplan / Job env before retrying a heavy TP Job."},"3389":{"id":"/contribute","page_id":"/contribute","type":"page","content":"Contribute","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Contribute"],"tags":["contributing","bazel","documentation"],"url":"/contribute"},"3390":{"id":"/contribute-0","page_id":"/contribute","tags":["contributing","bazel","documentation"],"type":"text","url":"/contribute","content":"Contributor path — devcontainer, Bazel, docs-as-code, and conventions for nvidia-dgx-spark-lab."},"3391":{"id":"/contribute-1","page_id":"/contribute","type":"heading","tags":["contributing","bazel","documentation"],"url":"/contribute#contribute","content":"Contribute"},"3392":{"id":"/contribute-2","page_id":"/contribute","type":"heading","tags":["contributing","bazel","documentation"],"url":"/contribute#setup","content":"Setup"},"3393":{"id":"/contribute-3","page_id":"/contribute","type":"heading","tags":["contributing","bazel","documentation"],"url":"/contribute#daily-targets","content":"Daily targets"},"3394":{"id":"/contribute-4","page_id":"/contribute","type":"heading","tags":["contributing","bazel","documentation"],"url":"/contribute#docs-contract","content":"Docs contract"},"3395":{"id"